[00:46.91] I roll the window down
[00:52.49] And then begin to breathe in
[01:06.11] The darkest country road
[01:10.73] And the strong scent of evergreen
[01:15.07] From the passenger seat as
[01:18.75] You are driving me home
[01:24.72] Then looking upwards
[01:29.52] I strain my eyes and try
[01:42.68] To tell the difference between
[01:47.79] Shooting stars and satellites
[01:52.30] From the passenger seat as
[01:55.83] You are driving me home
[02:01.36] Do they collide?
[02:05.96] I ask and you smile
[02:14.99] With my feet on the dash
[02:19.93] The world doesn't matter
[02:32.08] When you feel embarrassed
[02:36.19] Then I'll be your pride
[02:41.26] When you need directions
[02:45.73] Then I'll be the guide
[02:50.43] For all time
